On 2007-08-12, Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
> I think this has been mentioned here before, but cannot find it.
> What's that message supposed to tell me...?
> "You aren't sure you're doing this the right way..."

If you're unskilled or restricted in a weapon, you have a hard 75% cap
on your "to hit" chance.  If the cap is in effect (ie. your chances
would have been greater than 75%), then the message will display on a
1/3 chance. 

> It pops up if my human tourist hits with a wielded elven dagger
> (unskilled), while it doesn't if I hit (unskilled) bare handed.

Daggers get a +2 bonus to hit, while I suspect bare-handed unskilled
actually gets a penalty.  My guess is you're barely at 80% with the
dagger, and as such the game needs to warn you that you're suffering a
penalty and need to #enhance the skill.

You will never see this message once you're at Basic or better.

> Somewhat annoying to be constantly told that I am doing something
> wrong. The game wants to teach me something? Bah! :-/

Remember, "You" in-game usually refers to the character, not the 
actual human behind the keys.  Hence "You are hit", "You don't feel
cold", etc. ad nauseam.  The game isn't telling you-the-player that
you're doing something wrong... it's warning you-the-PC that you need to
#enhance the skill.

It is very similar to the monk's "...cumbersome" penalty messages 
while wearing body armor. 

